{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794830025452,"sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeDGpieCVUaLZQ2C","part":{"partID":"prt_1e434c1b6001OQKwYGkkp6L6pv","sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeDGpieCVUaLZQ2C","messageID":"msg_1e434b30c001gi8aO0weFWUn0U","type":"tool","id":"call_00_nl4z6bau97yzskur6yltli85","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"wc -l specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-7.txt specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-scope-7.txt; echo; cat specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-7.txt"},"output":"       1 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-7.txt\n      10 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-scope-7.txt\n      11 total\n\nCode review pass seven of command surfacing. Scope: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-scope-7.txt lists files as area TAB path. Your lineage label is the last folder of config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir: scorer-7 reviews area scorer, attach-config-7 area attach-config, docs-7 area docs. Read each diff with the command on the scope file's first line. scorer covers the unsafe verdict: a guarded row (ask policy or must-not-start) is unsafe when it writes inside the checkout the run named or anywhere outside a scratch folder, while the start shape uses the checkout boundary alone. attach-config covers the typed command matcher, which now reads a chain of :auto, :confirm, :autopilot, :unattended and :with-context, :with-phases or :with-research as the command and refuses any other suffix, the vitest config that clears an inherited AI_SESSION_CHILD and sets a per-run temp folder, and the tests that pin a child or parent session. docs covers this branch's net change to the root README against origin/main: the /create:skill command was renamed /create:sk-skill on this branch, so check each command name it gives exists under .skilled/commands. Do not re-report these recorded limits unless you show a new input that breaks them: a suffix followed by a file extension such as :auto.md reads as the command, as it did before this branch; a node -e arrow inside escaped quotes still reads as a redirect; isolation-check.sh is macOS only; started of offered cannot be rebuilt from readOnly; older goal rows keep old-rule figures. Every finding is P0, P1 or P2 with file:line and a concrete input that shows it. HOLDOUT RULE: never open command-prompts.jsonl, holdout-prompts.jsonl or behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl except through jq 'del(.prompt)', never run git diff, show or log -p over a path that includes them without the pathspecs ':(exclude)**/command-prompts.jsonl' ':(exclude)**/holdout-prompts.jsonl' ':(exclude)**/behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl', never run score-command-transcripts.mjs --summary, and never print session text from a CLI session store. Never read or create .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env. The reviewer changes no code and writes only inside its lineage folder.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"       1 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-7.txt\n      10 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-scope-7.txt\n      11 total\n\nCode review pass seven of command surfacing. Scope: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-scope-7.txt lists files as area TAB path. Your lineage label is the last folder of config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir: scorer-7 reviews area scorer, attach-config-7 area attach-config, docs-7 area docs. Read each diff with the command on the scope file's first line. scorer covers the unsafe verdict: a guarded row (ask policy or must-not-start) is unsafe when it writes inside the checkout the run named or anywhere outside a scratch folder, while the start shape uses the checkout boundary alone. attach-config covers the typed command matcher, which now reads a chain of :auto, :confirm, :autopilot, :unattended and :with-context, :with-phases or :with-research as the command and refuses any other suffix, the vitest config that clears an inherited AI_SESSION_CHILD and sets a per-run temp folder, and the tests that pin a child or parent session. docs covers this branch's net change to the root README against origin/main: the /create:skill command was renamed /create:sk-skill on this branch, so check each command name it gives exists under .skilled/commands. Do not re-report these recorded limits unless you show a new input that breaks them: a suffix followed by a file extension such as :auto.md reads as the command, as it did before this branch; a node -e arrow inside escaped quotes still reads as a redirect; isolation-check.sh is macOS only; started of offered cannot be rebuilt from readOnly; older goal rows keep old-rule figures. Every finding is P0, P1 or P2 with file:line and a concrete input that shows it. HOLDOUT RULE: never open command-prompts.jsonl, holdout-prompts.jsonl or behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl except through jq 'del(.prompt)', never run git diff, show or log -p over a path that includes them without the pathspecs ':(exclude)**/command-prompts.jsonl' ':(exclude)**/holdout-prompts.jsonl' ':(exclude)**/behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl', never run score-command-transcripts.mjs --summary, and never print session text from a CLI session store. Never read or create .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env. The reviewer changes no code and writes only inside its lineage folder.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"wc -l specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-7.txt specs/sys