iter lands in group 1 rather than in a body. Checked the packet registry for an existing finding with this input; the recorded heredoc finding names a delimiter that is not a bare identifier, a different input.\",\"dimension\":\"correctness\",\"downgradeTrigger\":\"Downgrade to ruled-out if the corpus and runner never emit a shell command with more than one heredoc delimiter on one line.\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:752\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:269\"],\"file\":\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:752\",\"finalSeverity\":\"P2\",\"findingClass\":\"correctness\",\"id\":\"iter1-P2-second-heredoc-body-write\",\"scopeProof\":\"The pattern, its redirect consumer and the shell write scanner are all inside the pass-six scoped scorer file.\",\"severity\":\"P2\",\"title\":\"A second heredoc on one opening line is not stripped, so its body comparison becomes a write\"},{\"affectedSurfaceHints\":[\"writePaths\",\"firstWritePosition\",\"insideCheckout\",\"startShape\",\"startRate\",\"startShapes.readWrite\"],\"alternativeExplanation\":\"A write with no named target is still a write, so counting it may be the conservative choice; that choice is conservative for unsafe but not for the start rule, where phase 036 defines the start as a write inside the checkout and an unknown folder is not evidence of one.\",\"claim\":\"writePaths keeps a write with no target as [null], and firstWritePosition skips a write only when its path is a string outside the checkout, so an unnamed write satisfies the inside-checkout test that startShape uses for readWrite.\",\"confidence\":0.85,\"counterevidenceSought\":\"Probed a Read of the command document plus a Write tool call with no path key, and a Read plus a Bash apply_patch whose body used ---/+++ headers; both produced one unnamed write and startState returned readWrite with started true. Checked whether any later step removes the unnamed write before the boundary; none does.\",\"dimension\":\"correctness\",\"downgradeTrigger\":\"Downgrade to ruled-out if every scoped runtime always records a target for a write tool call and for apply_patch.\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:327\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:729\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1513\"],\"file\":\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:327\",\"finalSeverity\":\"P2\",\"findingClass\":\"correctness\",\"id\":\"iter1-P2-unnamed-write-is-inside-checkout\",\"scopeProof\":\"writePaths, firstWritePosition and startShape are the scoped scorer own boundary path, and the phase 036 edge-case row names the outside-checkout write as a lookup.\",\"severity\":\"P2\",\"title\":\"A write whose target is never named counts as inside the checkout, so a lookup plus an unnamed write scores as a readWrite start\"}],\"findingsCount\":2,\"findingsNew\":[\"iter1-P2-second-heredoc-body-write\",\"iter1-P2-unnamed-write-is-inside-checkout\"],\"findingsSummary\":{\"P0\":0,\"P1\":0,\"P2\":2},\"focus\":\"correctness -- heredoc redirect stripping and the read-alone start rule\",\"generation\":1,\"graphEvents\":[{\"id\":\"file-scorer\",\"kind\":\"FILE\",\"label\":\"score-command-transcripts.mjs\",\"type\":\"node\"},{\"id\":\"bug-second-heredoc-body\",\"kind\":\"BUG_CLASS\",\"label\":\"second heredoc body left in the redirect scan\",\"type\":\"node\"},{\"id\":\"bug-unnamed-write-boundary\",\"kind\":\"BUG_CLASS\",\"label\":\"unnamed write counted as inside the checkout\",\"type\":\"node\"},{\"id\":\"edge-1\",\"relation\":\"IN_FILE\",\"source\":\"bug-second-heredoc-body\",\"target\":\"file-scorer\",\"type\":\"edge\"},{\"id\":\"edge-2\",\"relation\":\"IN_FILE\",\"source\":\"bug-unnamed-write-boundary\",\"target\":\"file-scorer\",\"type\":\"edge\"}],\"iteration\":1,\"lineageMode\":\"new\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"newFindingsRatio\":1,\"noveltyJustification\":\"First iteration of the lineage: two findings, neither present in the packet registry by title or by input, weighted new 2 of weighted total 2.\",\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=review target_agent=deep-review\",\"run\":\"fanout-scorer-6-1794815529929-dybl7p\",\"sessionId\":\"fanout-scorer-6-1794815529929-dybl7p\",\"status\":\"complete\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-review\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-16T08:09:27Z\",\"traceabilityChecks\":{\"results\":[{\"applicable\":true,\"evidence\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1494-1518\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1504\"],\"gateClass\":\"hard\",\"protocolId\":\"spec_code\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"summary\":\"Phase 036 REQ-004 maps to the startState shape return and its cases; REQ-001 follows by construction, and its numeric restatement is not re-run because the brief forbids --summary.\"}]},\"type\":\"iteration\"}\n{\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"dimensions\":[\"security\",\"traceability\"],\"durationMs\":210000,\"filesReviewed\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1696-1717\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1723-1772\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:2036-2056\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:2590-2665\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1560-1585\",\".skilled/skills/