t; the recorded heredoc finding names a delimiter that is not a bare identifier, a different input.\",\"alternativeExplanation\":\"A shell that lists two heredocs on one line is uncommon and the pre-fix pattern behaved the same way, so the gap may be accepted as out of reach; that reading leaves the fix comment (a heredoc body is data) untrue for an input the pattern claims to strip, and the false write moves the first-write boundary.\",\"finalSeverity\":\"P2\",\"confidence\":0.9,\"downgradeTrigger\":\"Downgrade to ruled-out if the corpus and runner never emit a shell command with more than one heredoc delimiter on one line.\",\"findingClass\":\"correctness\",\"scopeProof\":\"The pattern, its redirect consumer and the shell write scanner are all inside the pass-six scoped scorer file.\",\"affectedSurfaceHints\":[\"HEREDOC_BODY\",\"redirectTargets\",\"shellWriteTargets\",\"firstWritePosition\",\"workflowPath\",\"startShape\"]},{\"id\":\"iter1-P2-unnamed-write-is-inside-checkout\",\"severity\":\"P2\",\"title\":\"A write whose target is never named counts as inside the checkout, so a lookup plus an unnamed write scores as a readWrite start\",\"dimension\":\"correctness\",\"file\":\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:327\",\"claim\":\"writePaths keeps a write with no target as [null], and firstWritePosition skips a write only when its path is a string outside the checkout, so an unnamed write satisfies the inside-checkout test that startShape uses for readWrite.\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:327\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:729\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1513\"],\"counterevidenceSought\":\"Probed a Read of the command document plus a Write tool call with no path key,