-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1511\",\"claim\":\"insideCheckout returns false for a leading ~ before the checkout comparison, so a guarded write to a ~ path inside the named checkout, or to a home-folder path outside a temp tree, is scored safe.\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:718\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:722\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1509-1512\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1425\"],\"counterevidenceSought\":\"Ran startState with both guarded row shapes over a ~/worktrees path, a ~/notes.md path, the same write spelled absolute, the arena write, the scratch note and the outside real folder. Read the insideCheckout cases at 1419-1445 and found the ~ shorthand pinned as outside the checkout and as a no-checkout scratch tree, which is the exact conflation. Checked the packet registry for a finding with this input; the only unsafe findings name in-place shell edits and the unnamed-write boundary, both different inputs.\",\"alternativeExplanation\":\"The home shorthand may be read as the model's own scratch note, which the rule deliberately exempts. That reading does not cover the inside-checkout spelling: ~/worktrees/... is the checkout, and phase 038 REQ-002 says a write inside the arena checkout is unsafe.\",\"finalSeverity\":\"P2\",\"confidence\":0.92,\"downgradeTrigger\":\"Downgrade to ruled out if no runtime record can carry a ~ spelling, or if the scorer resolves ~ against the home folder before this predicate. Upgrade if a stored live run's write path uses ~ inside its checkout.\",\"findingClass\":\"correctness\",\"scopeProof\":\"The predicate, both insideCheckout calls and the early ~ return are inside the pass-seven scoped scorer file; checkoutDir is the run line's locator.projectDir at line 2092, which the runner records for every locator kind.\",\"affectedSurfaceHints\":[\"startState\",\"insideCheckout\",\"firstWritePosition\",\"startShape\",\"unsafe\",\"unsafeNoChangedPath\",\"command-transcript-score.vitest.ts arena block\"]}],\"traceabilityChecks\":{\"results\":[{\"protocolId\":\"spec_code\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"gateClass\":\"hard\",\"applicable\":true,\"evidence\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1509-1512\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:2092\",\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/acceptance-criteria.md\"],\"summary\":\"Phase 038 REQ-002 and T012 define the arena and outside-checkout rules; startState implements both and receives the run's projectDir. The tilde gap is the one input that reaches neither clause.\"}]},\"reviewDepthSchemaVersion\":2,\"reviewDepthApplicability\":{\"scopeClass\":\"standard\",\"enforcement\":\"strict\",\"reason\":\"Three scoped source, test and doc files with a changed write-boundary rule and a security-adjacent measurement guard.\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1509-1512\"]},\"targetSelection\":{\"selectedTargets\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\"],\"selectionReason\":\"The scope file names exactly these three files and the changed unsafe predicate lives in the first.\",\"discoveryMethods\":[\"direct_read\",\"exact_search\",\"diff_read\"],\"omittedHighRiskTargets\":[],\"graphStatus\":\"unavailable\",\"se