{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794830711959,"sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeDGpieCVUaLZQ2C","part":{"partID":"prt_1e43f3b2f001vPwaVo0whwZJDT","sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeDGpieCVUaLZQ2C","messageID":"msg_1e43f1a4f001oqDMdyi3eexOzr","type":"tool","id":"call_00_3rimo4usu6djbvipz9ivsfzs","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-7/deep-review-strategy.md","oldString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Init read the brief, the scope file, the fan-out config and the phase 038 spec and acceptance criteria before choosing a focus.\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- None yet.","newString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Init read the brief, the scope file, the fan-out config and the phase 038 spec and acceptance criteria before choosing a focus.\n- Importing the scorer and running one `node --input-type=module -e` probe over eleven write paths turned the whole predicate into an observed unsafe table, without opening a prompt file or running `--summary` (iteration 1).\n- Reading `insideCheckout` and `firstWritePosition` side by side showed the new predicate is the checkout boundary plus the scratch fallback, while the start shape keeps the checkout boundary alone (iteration 1).\n- Reading the moved-run scratch file beside the fix commit checked which writes the first fix actually moved, and every one writes under `<checkout>` (iteration 1).\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- Expecting `~` to expand before the checkout comparison: `insideCheckout` returns false on the shorthand before it looks at `checkoutDir`, so the first clause is never reached (iteration 1).\n- Expecting the no-checkout fallback to treat only temp trees as scratch: it also treats a `~` path as scratch, so a home-folder write is safe for the second clause too (iteration 1)."},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-7/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-7/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-7/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-7/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-7/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -61,14 +61,18 @@\n <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n \n - Init read the brief, the scope file, the fan-out config and the phase 038 spec and acceptance criteria before choosing a focus.\n+- Importing the scorer and running one `node --input-type=module -e` probe over eleven write paths turned the whole predicate into an observed unsafe table, without opening a prompt file or running `--summary` (iteration 1).\n+- Reading `insideCheckout` and `firstWritePosition` side by side showed the new predicate is the checkout boundary plus the scratch fallback, while the start shape keeps the checkout boundary alone (iteration 1).\n+- Reading the moved-run scratch file beside the fix commit checked which writes the first fix actually moved, and every one writes under `<checkout>` (iteration 1).\n \n ---\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n \n-- None yet.\n+- Expecting `~` to expand before the checkout comparison: `insideCheckout` returns false on the shorthand before it looks at `checkoutDir`, so the first clause is never reached (iteration 1).\n+- Expecting the no-checkout fallback to treat only temp trees as scratch: it also treats a `~` path as scratch, so a home-folder write is safe for the second clause too (iteration 1).\n \n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n","status":"modified","additions":5,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-7/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-7/deep-review-strategy.md\", \"oldString\": \"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n- Init read the brief, the scope file, the fan-out config and the phase 038 spec and acceptance criteria before choosing a focus.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- None yet.\", \"newString\": \"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n- Init read the brief, the scope file, the fan-out config and the phase 038 spec and acceptance criteria before choosing a focus.\\n- Importing the scorer and running one `node --input-type=module -e` probe over eleven write paths turned the whole predicate into an observed unsafe table, without opening a prompt file or running `--summary` (iteration 1).\\n- Reading `insideCheckout` and `firstWritePosition` side by side showed the new predicate is the checkout boundary plus the scratch fallback, while the start shape keeps the checkout boundary alone (iteration 1).\\n- Reading the moved-run scratch file beside the fix commit checked which writes the first fix actually moved, and every one writes under `<checkout>` (iteration 1).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- Expecting `~` to expand before the checkout comparison: `insideCheckout` returns false on the shorthand before it looks at `checkoutDir`, so the first clause is never reached (iteration 1).\\n- Expecting the no-checkout fallback to treat only temp trees as scratch: it also treats a `~` path as scratch, so a home-folder write is safe for the second clause too (iteration 1).\"}"},"time":{"start":1794830711599,"end":1794830711959}}}}
