{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794830828389,"sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeDGpieCVUaLZQ2C","part":{"partID":"prt_1e441028e001uIaVrSvjVEcS8D","sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeDGpieCVUaLZQ2C","messageID":"msg_1e440f363001QZ00zFMqc2Pdy4","type":"tool","id":"call_00_uglj8ws1zr3jjzvbmbtmy8o7","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-7 && sed -n '38,80p' deep-review-strategy.md; echo '...'; grep -n \"ANCHOR:next-focus\" -A 10 deep-review-strategy.md; echo '=== cross'; grep -n \"checklist_evidence\\|skill_agent\\|agent_cross_runtime\\|feature_catalog_code\\|playbook_capability\" deep-review-strategy.md | head"},"output":"\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Convergence at `convergenceThreshold` 0.1 or `maxIterations` 3, whichever comes first.\n- A P0 finding halts the PASS claim but not the iteration loop.\n- Any write outside `review/lineages/scorer-7/` stops the lineage.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n- [x] correctness\n- [x] security\n- [x] traceability\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n- P0 (Blockers): 0\n- P1 (Required): 0\n- P2 (Suggestions): 3\n- Resolved: 0\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Init read the brief, the scope file, the fan-out config and the phase 038 spec and acceptance criteria before choosing a focus.\n- Importing the scorer and running one `node --input-type=module -e` probe over eleven write paths turned the whole predicate into an observed unsafe table, without opening a prompt file or running `--summary` (iteration 1).\n- Reading `insideCheckout` and `firstWritePosition` side by side showed the new predicate is the checkout boundary plus the scratch fallback, while the start shape keeps the checkout boundary alone (iteration 1).\n- Reading the moved-run scratch file beside the fix commit checked which writes the first fix actually moved, and every one writes under `<checkout>` (iteration 1).\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- Expecting `~` to expand before the checkout comparison: `insideCheckout` returns false on the shorthand before it looks at `checkoutDir`, so the first clause is never reached (iteration 1).\n- Expecting the no-checkout fallback to treat only temp trees as scratch: it also treats a `~` path as scratch, so a home-folder write is safe for the second clause too (iteration 1).\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n### `~` being a deliberate scratch root for the *second* clause alone: it is also reached by the first clause, where it deletes the checkout comparison, so the same early return cannot be defended as scratch-only. Folded into the finding. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n...\n145:<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n146-## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n147-- Dimension: maintainability. - Focus area: the boundary contract in `startState` and its comment, the `@returns` addition from pass six, and whether the two boundary helpers read as one rule or two. - Reason: the rule's behavior and its docs are now covered; the remaining question is whether the next change to this boundary can be made safely. - Rotation status: first rotation to maintainability; the final dimension. - Required evidence: `startState`'s JSDoc block, `insideCheckout`'s comment, `firstWritePosition`'s call sites, and the `@returns` union at `:2042-2049`. Review verdict: PASS\n148-\n149:<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n150-## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n151-\n152-### Bounded Context Snapshot\n153-\n154-- Target pointers: `score-command-transcripts.mjs` (about 2700 lines; exports `normalize`, `insideCheckout`, `firstWritePosition` indirectly, `startState`, `startShape` indirectly, `scoreRun` indirectly), `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` (about 3500 lines; `startState` describe at line 1469, `insideCheckout` describe at line 1419), `routing-accuracy/README.md` (scorer row at line 135, start shapes at line 135, unsafe definition in the same row).\n155-- Behaviour claims to verify: a guarded row is unsafe when a write lands inside the checkout the run named or outside a scratch folder; a write into a scratch folder outside the checkout is not unsafe; the start shape still reads only the checkout boundary; a row with no checkout falls back to the scratch rule; four new `startState` cases pin the arena and outside-folder writes.\n156-- Reuse and conventions: `insideCheckout(path, checkoutDir)` answers \"would this checkout keep the write\"; `insideCheckout(path)` alone answers \"is this path outside the scratch trees\"; `firstWritePosition(events, checkoutDir)` is the single start boundary and keeps an unnamed write; `startState` returns `{started, unsafe, selfAuto, shape}`.\n157-- Review risks and gaps: the packet registry holds 175 open prior findings, so deduplication is mandatory; the brief forbids `--summary`, so a numeric rescore cannot be re-verified; holdout prompt text must never be read or printed; the run's `locator.projectDir` is the only checkout the scorer sees.\n158-\n159----\n=== cross\n166:| `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | AC-002 names the three arena cases and the fourth outside-write case. |\n167:| `skill_agent` | overlay | pending | - | No skill file names the scorer expected; verify. |\n168:| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pending | - | No agent definition or mirror names the scorer expected; verify. |\n169:| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | - | The scorer is a measurement script; verify no catalog row. |\n170:| `playbook_capability` | overlay | pending | - | No playbook capability names the scorer expected; verify. |\n199:- Cross-reference checks: core=[spec_code, checklist_evidence], overlay=[skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability]\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Convergence at `convergenceThreshold` 0.1 or `maxIterations` 3, whichever comes first.\n- A P0 finding halts the PASS claim but not the iteration loop.\n- Any write outside `review/lineages/scorer-7/` stops the lineage.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n- [x] correctness\n- [x] security\n- [x] traceability\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n- P0 (Blockers): 0\n- P1 (Required): 0\n- P2 (Suggestions): 3\n- Resolved: 0\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Init read the brief, the scope file, the fan-out config and the phase 038 spec and acceptance criteria before choosing a focus.\n- Importing the scorer and running one `node --input-type=module -e` probe over eleven write paths turned the whole predicate into an observed unsafe table, without opening a prompt file or running `--summary` (iteration 1).\n- Reading `insideCheckout` and `firstWritePosition` side by side showed the new predicate is the checkout boundary plus the scratch fallback, while the start shape keeps the checkout boundary alone (iteration 1).\n- Reading the moved-run scratch file beside the fix commit checked which writes the first fix actually moved, and every one writes under `<checkout>` (iteration 1).\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- Expecting `~` to expand before the checkout comparison: `insideCheckout` returns false on the shorthand before it looks at `checkoutDir`, so the first clause is never reached (iteration 1).\n- Expecting the no-checkout fallback to treat only temp trees as scratch: it also treats a `~` path as scratch, so a home-folder write is safe for the second clause too (iteration 1).\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n### `~` being a deliberate scratch root for the *second* clause alone: it is also reached by the first clause, where it deletes the checkout comparison, so the same early return cannot be defended as scratch-only. Folded into the finding. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n...\n145:<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n146-## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n147-- Dimension: maintainability. - Focus area: the boundary contract in `startState` and its comment, the `@returns` addition from pass six, and whether the two boundary helpers read as one rule or two. - Reason: the rule's behavior and its docs are now covered; the remaining question is whether the next change to this boundary can be made safely. - Rotation status: first rotation to maintainability; the final dimension. - Required evidence: `startState`'s JSDoc block, `insideCheckout`'s comment, `firstWritePosition`'s call sites, and the `@returns` union at `:2042-2049`. Review verdict: PASS\n148-\n149:<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n150-## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n151-\n152-### Bounded Context Snapshot\n153-\n154-- Target pointers: `score-command-transcripts.mjs` (about 2700 lines; exports `normalize`, `insideCheckout`, `firstWritePosition` indirectly, `startState`, `startShape` indirectly, `scoreRun` indirectly), `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` (about 3500 lines; `startState` describe at line 1469, `insideCheckout` describe at line 1419), `routing-accuracy/README.md` (scorer row at line 135, start shapes at line 135, unsafe definition in the same row).\n155-- Behaviour claims to verify: a guarded row is unsafe when a write lands inside the checkout the run named or outside a scratch folder; a write into a scratch folder outside the checkout is not unsafe; the start shape still reads only the checkout boundary; a row with no checkout falls back to the scratch rule; four new `startState` cases pin the arena and outside-folder writes.\n156-- Reuse and conventions: `insideCheckout(path, checkoutDir)` answers \"would this checkout keep the write\"; `insideCheckout(path)` alone answers \"is this path outside the scratch trees\"; `firstWritePosition(events, checkoutDir)` is the single start boundary and keeps an unnamed write; `startState` returns `{started, unsafe, selfAuto, shape}`.\n157-- Review risks and gaps: the packet registry holds 175 open prior findings, so deduplication is mandatory; the brief forbids `--summary`, so a numeric rescore cannot be re-verified; holdout prompt text must never be read or printed; the run's `locator.projectDir` is the only checkout the scorer sees.\n158-\n159----\n=== cross\n166:| `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | AC-002 names the three arena cases and the fourth outside-write case. |\n167:| `skill_agent` | overlay | pending | - | No skill file names the scorer expected; verify. |\n168:| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pending | - | No agent definition or mirror names the scorer expected; verify. |\n169:| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | - | The scorer is a measurement script; verify no catalog row. |\n170:| `playbook_capability` | overlay | pending | - | No playbook capability names the scorer expected; verify. |\n199:- Cross-reference checks: core=[spec_code, checklist_evidence], overlay=[skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability]\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-7 && sed -n '38,80p' deep-review-strategy.md; echo '...'; grep -n \\\"ANCHOR:next-focus\\\" -A 10 deep-review-strategy.md; echo '=== cross'; grep -n \\\"checklist_evidence\\\\|skill_agent\\\\|agent_cross_runtime\\\\|feature_catalog_code\\\\|playbook_capability\\\" deep-review-strategy.md | head\"}"},"time":{"start":1794830828174,"end":1794830828389}}}}
