{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794830841206,"sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeDGpieCVUaLZQ2C","part":{"partID":"prt_1e44133f3001MinndaIbsDZCNT","sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeDGpieCVUaLZQ2C","messageID":"msg_1e4410d62001FZQCJe52Cmq2BF","type":"tool","id":"call_00_urqk8e7c8767c89bvnypya2q","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"- Reading the moved-run scratch file beside the fix commit checked which writes the first fix actually moved, and every one writes under `<checkout>` (iteration 1).\n- Probing traversal spellings found the one escape the prefix tests allow and proved the checkout-side traversal stays conservative (iteration 2).\n- Grepping `.skilled` and `docs` for `unsafeNoChangedPath` in one call settled all four overlay protocols: the routing-accuracy README is the only doc that names the scorer (iteration 2).\n- Reading AC-002 beside `scratch/after-review.txt` checked the checklist evidence at the level the brief allows, without a rescore (iteration 2).\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- Expecting `~` to expand before the checkout comparison: `insideCheckout` returns false on the shorthand before it looks at `checkoutDir`, so the first clause is never reached (iteration 1).\n- Expecting the no-checkout fallback to treat only temp trees as scratch: it also treats a `~` path as scratch, so a home-folder write is safe for the second clause too (iteration 1).\n- Expecting the scratch prefix test to resolve a `..` segment: `/tmp/../Users/dev/repo/x.md` keeps the `/tmp/` prefix and is exempted, though it resolves to a real folder (iteration 2).\n- Expecting the README row to state the guarded-write rule: it defines every other field but only names the loop-without-init case, while its outside-write sentence says such a write sets no boundary (iteration 2).","oldString":"- Reading the moved-run scratch file beside the fix commit checked which writes the first fix actually moved, and every one writes under `<checkout>` (iteration 1).\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- Expecting `~` to expand before the checkout comparison: `insideCheckout` returns false on the shorthand before it looks at `checkoutDir`, so the first clause is never reached (iteration 1).\n- Expecting the no-checkout fallback to treat only temp trees as scratch: it also treats a `~` path as scratch, so a home-folder write is safe for the second clause too (iteration 1).","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-7/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-7/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-7/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-7/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-7/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-7/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -64,15 +64,20 @@\n - Init read the brief, the scope file, the fan-out config and the phase 038 spec and acceptance criteria before choosing a focus.\n - Importing the scorer and running one `node --input-type=module -e` probe over eleven write paths turned the whole predicate into an observed unsafe table, without opening a prompt file or running `--summary` (iteration 1).\n - Reading `insideCheckout` and `firstWritePosition` side by side showed the new predicate is the checkout boundary plus the scratch fallback, while the start shape keeps the checkout boundary alone (iteration 1).\n - Reading the moved-run scratch file beside the fix commit checked which writes the first fix actually moved, and every one writes under `<checkout>` (iteration 1).\n+- Probing traversal spellings found the one escape the prefix tests allow and proved the checkout-side traversal stays conservative (iteration 2).\n+- Grepping `.skilled` and `docs` for `unsafeNoChangedPath` in one call settled all four overlay protocols: the routing-accuracy README is the only doc that names the scorer (iteration 2).\n+- Reading AC-002 beside `scratch/after-review.txt` checked the checklist evidence at the level the brief allows, without a rescore (iteration 2).\n \n ---\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n \n - Expecting `~` to expand before the checkout comparison: `insideCheckout` returns false on the shorthand before it looks at `checkoutDir`, so the first clause is never reached (iteration 1).\n - Expecting the no-checkout fallback to treat only temp trees as scratch: it also treats a `~` path as scratch, so a home-folder write is safe for the second clause too (iteration 1).\n+- Expecting the scratch prefix test to resolve a `..` segment: `/tmp/../Users/dev/repo/x.md` keeps the `/tmp/` prefix and is exempted, though it resolves to a real folder (iteration 2).\n+- Expecting the README row to state the guarded-write rule: it defines every other field but only names the loop-without-init case, while its outside-write sentence says such a write sets no boundary (iteration 2).\n \n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n","status":"modified","additions":5,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-7/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\": \"- Reading the moved-run scratch file beside the fix commit checked which writes the first fix actually moved, and every one writes under `<checkout>` (iteration 1).\\n- Probing traversal spellings found the one escape the prefix tests allow and proved the checkout-side traversal stays conservative (iteration 2).\\n- Grepping `.skilled` and `docs` for `unsafeNoChangedPath` in one call settled all four overlay protocols: the routing-accuracy README is the only doc that names the scorer (iteration 2).\\n- Reading AC-002 beside `scratch/after-review.txt` checked the checklist evidence at the level the brief allows, without a rescore (iteration 2).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- Expecting `~` to expand before the checkout comparison: `insideCheckout` returns false on the shorthand before it looks at `checkoutDir`, so the first clause is never reached (iteration 1).\\n- Expecting the no-checkout fallback to treat only temp trees as scratch: it also treats a `~` path as scratch, so a home-folder write is safe for the second clause too (iteration 1).\\n- Expecting the scratch prefix test to resolve a `..` segment: `/tmp/../Users/dev/repo/x.md` keeps the `/tmp/` prefix and is exempted, though it resolves to a real folder (iteration 2).\\n- Expecting the README row to state the guarded-write rule: it defines every other field but only names the loop-without-init case, while its outside-write sentence says such a write sets no boundary (iteration 2).\", \"oldString\": \"- Reading the moved-run scratch file beside the fix commit checked which writes the first fix actually moved, and every one writes under `<checkout>` (iteration 1).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- Expecting `~` to expand before the checkout comparison: `insideCheckout` returns false on the shorthand before it looks at `checkoutDir`, so the first clause is never reached (iteration 1).\\n- Expecting the no-checkout fallback to treat only temp trees as scratch: it also treats a `~` path as scratch, so a home-folder write is safe for the second clause too (iteration 1).\", \"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-