{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794830973572,"sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeDGpieCVUaLZQ2C","part":{"partID":"prt_1e4433a6b002p8CIFB8vyEVVL5","sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeDGpieCVUaLZQ2C","messageID":"msg_1e4432d69001Krz82nxT4pEhk9","type":"tool","id":"call_00_3uuduv7os7nfsg1h44s1qn6p","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-6/review-report.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-6/review-report.md, lines 1-171\n1: # Review Report - Command Surfacing Pass Six, `scorer-6`\n2: \n3: Lineage: `fanout-scorer-6-1794815529929-dybl7p` | Artifact root: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-6` | Stop reason: `maxIterationsReached` | Iterations: 3\n4: \n5: ## 1. Executive Summary\n6: \n7: **Overall verdict: PASS (advisories only)**\n8: \n9: - hasAdvisories: true\n10: - Active findings: P0 = 0, P1 = 0, P2 = 4\n11: - Review scope: the three files `review/review-scope-6.txt` assigns to area `scorer` — the transcript scorer, its vitest file, and the routing-accuracy README row and paragraph that describe it.\n12: - Dimensions covered: correctness (iteration 1), security and traceability (iteration 2, one cross-reference pass), maintainability (iteration 3).\n13: - Operator review focus: \"Review pass six. First read specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-6.txt and follow it: it names your area by lineage label, the scope file review/review-scope-6.txt, the diff command for each area, the recorded limits not to re-report and the holdout rule. Every finding is P0, P1 or P2 with file:line and a concrete input. Change no code and write only inside your lineage folder.\"\n14: \n15: The pass-six change is sound where it matters. `redirectTargets` now strips a heredoc body before it scans for `>`, an empty body ends at its own end line, and a backslash-quoted end word is honoured; `startState` returns a shape and counts a read with no checkout write as `readOnly` rather than a start; `startShapes` sums to `started` over the same uncapped start-row set. Every new case is pinned by a test, and the packet's 036 evidence files carry the counts its criteria name.\n16: \n17: Four P2 advisories remain. Two are residual holes in the changed logic: a second heredoc listed on one opening line leaves its body scannable, and a write whose target the transcript never names passes the inside-checkout test, so a lookup can still be scored as a start. One is stale documentation in the same README row and in a test comment, both still saying a bare document read is a start. One is the `scoreRun` return declaration, which omits the `startShape` field its consumer reads.\n18: \n19: ## 2. Planning Trigger\n20: \n21: `/speckit:plan` is not required: no active P1 or P0 finding and no failed quality gate. The follow-on is `/create:changelog`, and the four advisories are optional cleanup for the next pass over the scorer.\n22: \n23: ```json\n24: {\n25:   \"triggered\": false,\n26:   \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n27:   \"hasAdvisories\": true,\n28:   \"activeFindings\": {\"P0\": 0, \"P1\": 0, \"P2\": 4},\n29:   \"followOn\": \"/create:changelog\",\n30:   \"remediationWorkstreams\": [\n31:     \"WS-1 heredoc and write-boundary completeness\",\n32:     \"WS-2 docs and contract drift\",\n33:     \"WS-3 optional: one shared shape key list\"\n34:   ],\n35:   \"specSeed\": [],\n36:   \"planSeed\": [\n37:     \"Strip every heredoc delimiter on an opening line, or strip the pairs in document order\",\n38:     \"Treat an unnamed write as neither an inside nor an outside write for the start boundary\",\n39:     \"Delete the stale cat-counts sentence from the README and the shell-step test comment\",\n40:     \"Add startShape to the scoreRun return declaration and key the tally from one shape list\"\n41:   ],\n42:   \"findingClasses\": [\"correctness\", \"traceability\", \"maintainability\"],\n43:   \"affectedSurfacesSeed\": [\n44:     \"score-command-transcripts.mjs HEREDOC_BODY/redirectTargets\",\n45:     \"score-command-transcripts.mjs writePaths/firstWritePosition/startShape\",\n46:     \"routing-accuracy/README.md scorer row\",\n47:     \"command-transcript-score.vitest.ts shell-step table\",\n48:     \"score-command-transcripts.mjs scoreRun @returns/addScored\"\n49:   ],\n50:   \"fixCompletenessRequired\": false\n51: }\n52: ```\n53: \n54: ## 3. Active Finding Registry\n55: \n56: | ID | Severity | Title | Dimension | Evidence | Fix recommendation | Finding class | Scope proof | Affected surfaces |\n57: |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n58: | iter1-P2-second-heredoc-body-write | P2 | A second heredoc on one opening line is not stripped, so its body comparison becomes a write | correctness | `score-command-transcripts.mjs:752`, `:269-300` | Consume every delimiter on the opening line, or strip each heredoc pair in document order | correctness | Pattern, redirect consumer and shell write scanner are all in the scoped scorer | `HEREDOC_BODY`, `redirectTargets`, `shellWriteTargets`, `firstWritePosition`, `workflowPath`, `startShape` |\n59: | iter1-P2-unnamed-write-is-inside-checkout | P2 | A write whose target is never named counts as inside the checkout, so a lookup plus an unnamed write scores as a `readWrite` start | correctness | `score-command-transcripts.mjs:327`, `:729-736`, `:1513-1518` | Count an unnamed write for `unsafe` only, never for the checkout boundary | correctness | Boundary path is the scoped scorer's own, and phase 036 names the outside-checkout write as a lookup | `writePaths`, `firstWritePosition`, `insideCheckout`, `startShape`, `startRate`, `startShapes.readWrite` |\n60: | iter2-P2-old-start-rule-still-stated | P2 | The README and the shell-step test still say a bare document read is a start | traceability | `routing-accuracy/README.md:135`, `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1565-1579` | Delete the `cat` clause from both sentences and keep the search, in-place `sed` and heredoc exclusions | traceability | Both files are pass-six scoped, and the contradiction is inside one README row | `startRate`, `startShapes.readOnly`, `readDocument`, `startShape`, README scorer row, shell-step test comment |\n61: | iter3-P2-score-run-return-omits-start-shape | P2 | `scoreRun`'s declared return type omits `startShape`, the field `addScored` reads | maintainability | `score-command-transcripts.mjs:2035-2041`, `:2104`, `:2412` | Add the field to the union and key the tally from one shape list | maintainability | Declaration, field and consumer are all in the scoped scorer | `scoreRun` `@returns`, `addScored`, `startShapes`, `newTally` |\n62: \n63: Every finding above is active. No finding was downgraded or resolved during the run, and none duplicates a registry finding by title or by input; the `$'EOF'` heredoc form and the shell-read-as-load gap were recognised as already recorded and left out of this report.\n64: \n65: ## 4. Remediation Workstreams\n66: \n67: ### WS-1 Heredoc and write-boundary completeness (P2, advisory)\n68: 1. Make `HEREDOC_BODY`'s opening-line group stop at the last delimiter on the line, so `cat <<A <<B` consumes both bodies; add the two-delimiter case to the existing `it.each` table.\n69: 2. Decide the unnamed-write rule once: it should stay a write for `unsafe` and stop being evidence of an inside-checkout write for `startShape`, with one case per unnamed-write producer (`apply_patch` with no header, a write tool call with no path).\n70: \n71: ### WS-2 Docs and contract drift (P2, advisory)\n72: 1. Remove \"a `cat` of the command's document counts\" from the README row and from the comment above the shell-step table; the surrounding exclusions stay correct.\n73: 2. Add `startShape` to `scoreRun`'s `@returns` union.\n74: \n75: ### WS-3 Optional: one shared shape key list (P2 follow-on)\n76: 1. Export the five shape names from one place and build `newTally().startShapes` from it, so a renamed shape cannot print an `undefined` key.\n77: \n78: ## 5. Spec Seed\n79: \n80: No spec is owed for this lineage: the four findings are advisories and phase 036's requirements are met at code level. If a later packet picks them up, its scope is the three scoped files plus the packet's 036 edge-case row, and its behaviour contract is:\n81: \n82: - A heredoc body is data for every heredoc on the opening line, not only the first.\n83: - A start requires a write the run's own checkout would keep; an unnamed write is not that evidence.\n84: - Every printed start number and the README that describes it state the same rule.\n85: \n86: ## 6. Plan Seed\n87: \n88: 1. Extend the heredoc stripper to multi-delimiter opening lines and add the case to `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts`.\n89: 2. Split the unnamed write from the checkout boundary in `startShape`, with one test per producer.\n90: 3. Delete the stale `cat` sentence from the README and the shell-step comment.\n91: 4. Add `startShape` to the `scoreRun` declaration and, optionally, one exported shape list.\n92: \n93: ## 7. Traceability Status\n94: \n95: ### Core Protocols\n96: \n97: | Protocol | Status | Iteration | Evidence | Notes |\n98: |---|---|---|---|---|\n99: | `spec_code` | pass | 1, 2, 3 | `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1494-1518`, `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1504` | Phase 036 REQ-004 maps to the shape return and its cases; REQ-001 holds by construction. The numeric restatement is not re-run because the brief forbids `--summary`. |\n100: | `checklist_evidence` | pass | 2, 3 | `036-start-rate-fixed-rule/scratch/restate.txt`, `scratch/restate-sets.txt`, `scratch/after.txt`, `035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/scratch/shape-check.txt` | The cited files carry the 22 start lines, the 10 decline lines, the 11 pre/final data lines, the 2326-passed suite line and the mutation check of the new summary case. |\n101: \n102: ### Overlay Protocols\n103: \n104: | Protocol | Status | Iteration | Reason |\n105: |---|---|---|---|\n106: | `skill_agent` | notApplicable | 3 | No skill file under `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor` names the scorer; only the folder README does. |\n107: | `agent_cross_runtime` | notApplicable | 3 | No agent definition in `.skilled/agents/` or a runtime mirror names the scorer. |\n108: | `feature_catalog_code` | notApplicable | 3 | The scorer is a measurement script with no catalog row. |\n109: | `playbook_capability` | notApplicable | 3 | No playbook capability names the scorer. |\n110: \n111: ### AC_COVERAGE\n112: \n113: Advisory and not machine-run by this lineage: `validate.sh` is outside the permitted commands for a detached lineage. Read by hand, every 036 acceptance row is `Met` with the evidence this report cites, so the signal is expected to pass when the packet is validated at the merge.\n114: \n115: ## 8. Deferred Items\n116: \n117: - The numeric restatement of 007 and 033 is accepted from the packet's own `scratch/` evidence, not re-scored here.\n118: - The duplicated start rule (`startShape` versus `startedCommand`) is recorded as a follow-on risk, not a finding: the two agree today and two instances do not justify a shared helper under the repository's restraint rule.\n119: - A missing fresh row file makes the scorer file fresh runs as `unknown_row` rather than refusing; that path predates this branch and is recorded here, not raised.\n120: \n121: ## Dimension Expansion Map\n122: \n123: | Dimension | Iterations | Result |\n124: |---|---|---|\n125: | correctness | 1 | Two P2: multi-heredoc false write; unnamed write counted as inside the checkout |\n126: | security | 2 | No finding: holdout rows are refused before a session loads, and no printed line carries prompt text |\n127: | traceability | 2 | One P2: the old cat-counts rule survives in the README row and the shell-step comment |\n128: | maintainability | 3 | One P2: `scoreRun`'s return declaration omits `startShape` |\n129: \n130: ## 9. Search Ledger\n131: \n132: | Search | Method | Result | Disposition |\n133: |---|---|---|---|\n134: | Heredoc stripping and redirect scanning | direct read + `node --input-type=module -e` probe over `normalize` | Empty body, backslash end word and opening-line redirect behave as documented; a two-delimiter line leaves the second body scannable | finding `iter1-P2-second-heredoc-body-write` |\n135: | Write boundary and the read-alone rule | direct read + probe over `startState`/`startedCommand` | A read plus an unnamed write returns `readWrite`; a read plus an outside-checkout write returns `readOnly` | finding `iter1-P2-unnamed-write-is-inside-checkout`; the outside-checkout case ruled in favour of the code |\n136: | Start-shape tally invariant | direct read of `scoreRun`, `addScored`, `tallyBlock` | The four starting shapes sum to `started`; `readOnly` holds the lookups | clean |\n137: | Holdout hygiene | direct read of `loadRowLabels`, `scoreRun`, every `process.stdout.write` line | Holdout rows are marked and refused before a session loads; output carries ids, codes and counts | clean |\n138: | Docs against code | read of the README row and the shell-step comment | Both keep the old rule in one place | finding `iter2-P2-old-start-rule-still-stated` |\n139: | Packet checklist evidence | read of the 036 and 035 `scratch/` files | Counts match the criteria's data lines; mutation check recorded | clean |\n140: | Producer/consumer contract | read of `scoreRun`'s `@returns`, the object it builds and `addScored` | `startShape` is missing from the declaration | finding `iter3-P2-score-run-return-omits-start-shape` |\n141: \n142: ## 10. Audit Appendix\n143: \n144: ### Iteration Records\n145: \n146: | Iteration | Focus | Findings | Ratio | Verdict | Gateway receipt |\n147: |---|---|---|---|---|---|\n148: | 1 | correctness | 2 P2 | 1.0 | PASS | ledger sequence 2, `event-588468c9` |\n149: | 2 | security and traceability | 1 P2 | 0.3333 | PASS | ledger sequence 3, `event-96a8b6c6` |\n150: | 3 | maintainability | 1 P2 | 0.25 | PASS | ledger sequence 4, `event-5d31c238` |\n151: \n152: ### Core Protocols Appendix\n153: \n154: - `spec_code`: iteration 1 recorded the mapping from phase 036 REQ-004 to `startState` and its cases; iteration 3 re-read the same lines while checking the contract.\n155: - `checklist_evidence`: iteration 2 read the four `scratch/` files named by the 035 and 036 criteria; iteration 3 carried the result.\n156: \n157: ### Overlay Protocols Appendix\n158: \n159: - All four overlay protocols resolve `notApplicable` in iteration 3, each with the read that shows no skill, agent, catalog row or playbook capability names the scorer.\n160: \n161: ### State Integrity\n162: \n163: - Three iteration narratives, three delta files, three canonical records and three receipted ledger appends agree on iteration number, focus, dimension set and finding ids.\n164: - `deep-review-state.jsonl` is the gateway's projection; the lineage never wrote it directly.\n165: - The reducer ran after each iteration (exit 0) and owns the registry, the dashboard and the anchored strategy blocks.\n166: - The registry's `dimension` for `iter2-P2-old-start-rule-still-stated` reads `security` while its finding class is `traceability`: the reducer derives a finding's dimension from the first dimension name in the iteration focus, and iteration 2's focus names security first. The finding's own `dimension` and class in `findingDetails` and in `deltas/iter-002.jsonl` are `traceability`.\n167: - No file outside `review/lineages/scorer-6/` was created or modified by this lineage, and no review target file was touched; `git status --porcelain -- .skilled` is empty.\n168: \n169: ### Holdout Statement\n170: \n171: No corpus, holdout or fresh prompt file was opened by this lineage. The probes imported the scorer module and passed crafted records in memory; the only evidence reads were the packet's `scratch/` text files and the packet's acceptance criteria.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-6/review-report.md, lines 1-171\n1: # Review Report - Command Surfacing Pass Six, `scorer-6`\n2: \n3: Lineage: `fanout-scorer-6-1794815529929-dybl7p` | Artifact root: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-6` | Stop reason: `maxIterationsReached` | Iterations: 3\n4: \n5: ## 1. Executive Summary\n6: \n7: **Overall verdict: PASS (advisories only)**\n8: \n9: - hasAdvisories: true\n10: - Active findings: P0 = 0, P1 = 0, P2 = 4\n11: - Review scope: the three files `review/review-scope-6.txt` assigns to area `scorer` — the transcript scorer, its vitest file, and the routing-accuracy README row and paragraph that describe it.\n12: - Dimensions covered: correctness (iteration 1), security and traceability (iteration 2, one cross-reference pass), maintainability (iteration 3).\n13: - Operator review focus: \"Review pass six. First read specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-6.txt and follow it: it names your area by lineage label, the scope file review/review-scope-6.txt, the diff command for each area, the recorded limits not to re-report and the holdout rule. Every finding is P0, P1 or P2 with file:line and a concrete input. Change no code and write only inside your lineage folder.\"\n14: \n15: The pass-six change is sound where it matters. `redirectTargets` now strips a heredoc body before it scans for `>`, an empty body ends at its own end line, and a backslash-quoted end word is honoured; `startState` returns a shape and counts a read with no checkout write as `readOnly` rather than a start; `startShapes` sums to `started` over the same uncapped start-row set. Every new case is pinned by a test, and the packet's 036 evidence files carry the counts its criteria name.\n16: \n17: Four P2 advisories remain. Two are residual holes in the changed logic: a second heredoc listed on one opening line leaves its body scannable, and a write whose target the transcript never names passes the inside-checkout test, so a lookup can still be scored as a start. One is stale documentation in the same README row and in a test comment, both still saying a bare document read is a start. One is the `scoreRun` return declaration, which omits the `startShape` field its consumer reads.\n18: \n19: ## 2. Planning Trigger\n20: \n21: `/speckit:plan` is not required: no active P1 or P0 finding and no failed quality gate. The follow-on is `/create:changelog`, and the four advisories are optional cleanup for the next pass over the scorer.\n22: \n23: ```json\n24: {\n25:   \"triggered\": false,\n26:   \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n27:   \"hasAdvisories\": true,\n28:   \"activeFindings\": {\"P0\": 0, \"P1\": 0, \"P2\": 4},\n29:   \"followOn\": \"/create:changelog\",\n30:   \"remediationWorkstreams\": [\n31:     \"WS-1 heredoc and write-boundary completeness\",\n32:     \"WS-2 docs and contract drift\",\n33:     \"WS-3 optional: one shared shape key list\"\n34:   ],\n35:   \"specSeed\": [],\n36:   \"planSeed\": [\n37:     \"Strip every heredoc delimiter on an opening line, or strip the pairs in document order\",\n38:     \"Treat an unnamed write as neither an inside nor an outside write for the start boundary\",\n39:     \"Delete the stale cat-counts sentence from the README and the shell-step test comment\",\n40:     \"Add startShape to the scoreRun return declaration and key the tally from one shape list\"\n41:   ],\n42:   \"findingClasses\": [\"correctness\", \"traceability\", \"maintainability\"],\n43:   \"affectedSurfacesSeed\": [\n44:     \"score-command-transcripts.mjs HEREDOC_BODY/redirectTargets\",\n45:     \"score-command-transcripts.mjs writePaths/firstWritePosition/startShape\",\n46:     \"routing-accuracy/README.md scorer row\",\n47:     \"command-transcript-score.vitest.ts shell-step table\",\n48:     \"score-command-transcripts.mjs scoreRun @returns/addScored\"\n49:   ],\n50:   \"fixCompletenessRequired\": false\n51: }\n52: ```\n53: \n54: ## 3. Active Finding Registry\n55: \n56: | ID | Severity | Title | Dimension | Evidence | Fix recommendation | Finding class | Scope proof | Affected surfaces |\n57: |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n58: | iter1-P2-second-heredoc-body-write | P2 | A second heredoc on one opening line is not stripped, so its body comparison becomes a write | correctness | `score-command-transcripts.mjs:752`, `:269-300` | Consume every delimiter on the opening line, or strip each heredoc pair in document order | correctness | Pattern, redirect consumer and shell write scanner are all in the scoped scorer | `HEREDOC_BODY`, `redirectTargets`, `shellWriteTargets`, `firstWritePosition`, `workflowPath`, `startShape` |\n59: | iter1-P2-unnamed-write-is-inside-checkout | P2 | A write whose target is never named counts as inside the checkout, so a lookup plus an unnamed write scores as a `readWrite` start | correctness | `score-command-transcripts.mjs:327`, `:729-736`, `:1513-1518` | Count an unnamed write for `unsafe` only, never for the checkout boundary | correctness | Boundary path is the scoped scorer's own, and phase 036 names the outside-checkout write as a lookup | `writePaths`, `firstWritePosition`, `insideCheckout`, `startShape`, `startRate`, `startShapes.readWrite` |\n60: | iter2-P2-old-start-rule-still-stated | P2 | The README and the shell-step test still say a bare document read is a start | traceability | `routing-accuracy/README.md:135`, `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1565-1579` | Delete the `cat` clause from both sentences and keep the search, in-place `sed` and heredoc exclusions | traceability | Both files are pass-six scoped, and the contradiction is inside one README row | `startRate`, `startShapes.readOnly`, `readDocument`, `startShape`, README scorer row, shell-step test comment |\n61: | iter3-P2-score-run-return-omits-start-shape | P2 | `scoreRun`'s declared return type omits `startShape`, the field `addScored` reads | maintainability | `score-command-transcripts.mjs:2035-2041`, `:2104`, `:2412` | Add the field to the union and key the tally from one shape list | maintainability | Declaration, field and consumer are all in the scoped scorer | `scoreRun` `@returns`, `addScored`, `startShapes`, `newTally` |\n62: \n63: Every finding above is active. No finding was downgraded or resolved during the run, and none duplicates a registry finding by title or by input; the `$'EOF'` heredoc form and the shell-read-as-load gap were recognised as already recorded and left out of this report.\n64: \n65: ## 4. Remediation Workstreams\n66: \n67: ### WS-1 Heredoc and write-boundary completeness (P2, advisory)\n68: 1. Make `HEREDOC_BODY`'s opening-line group stop at the last delimiter on the line, so `cat <<A <<B` consumes both bodies; add the two-delimiter case to the existing `it.each` table.\n69: 2. Decide the unnamed-write rule once: it should stay a write for `unsafe` and stop being evidence of an inside-checkout write for `startShape`, with one case per unnamed-write producer (`apply_patch` with no header, a write tool call with no path).\n70: \n71: ### WS-2 Docs and contract drift (P2, advisory)\n72: 1. Remove \"a `cat` of the command's document counts\" from the README row and from the comment above the shell-step table; the surrounding exclusions stay correct.\n73: 2. Add `startShape` to `scoreRun`'s `@returns` union.\n74: \n75: ### WS-3 Optional: one shared shape key list (P2 follow-on)\n76: 1. Export the five shape names from one place and build `newTally().startShapes` from it, so a renamed shape cannot print an `undefined` key.\n77: \n78: ## 5. Spec Seed\n79: \n80: No spec is owed for this lineage: the four findings are advisories and phase 036's requirements are met at code level. If a later packet picks them up, its scope is the three scoped files plus the packet's 036 edge-case row, and its behaviour contract is:\n81: \n82: - A heredoc body is data for every heredoc on the opening line, not only the first.\n83: - A start requires a write the run's own checkout would keep; an unnamed write is not that evidence.\n84: - Every printed start number and the README that describes it state the same rule.\n85: \n86: ## 6. Plan Seed\n87: \n88: 1. Extend the heredoc stripper to multi-delimiter opening lines and add the case to `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts`.\n89: 2. Split the unnamed write from the checkout boundary in `startShape`, with one test per producer.\n90: 3. Delete the stale `cat` sentence from the README and the shell-step comment.\n91: 4. Add `startShape` to the `scoreRun` declaration and, optionally, one exported shape list.\n92: \n93: ## 7. Traceability Status\n94: \n95: ### Core Protocols\n96: \n97: | Protocol | Status | Iteration | Evidence | Notes |\n98: |---|---|---|---|---|\n99: | `spec_code` | pass | 1, 2, 3 | `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1494-1518`, `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1504` | Phase 036 REQ-004 maps to the shape return and its cases; REQ-001 holds by construction. The numeric restatement is not re-run because the brief forbids `--summary`. |\n100: | `checklist_evidence` | pass | 2, 3 | `036-start-rate-fixed-rule/scratch/restate.txt`, `scratch/restate-sets.txt`, `scratch/after.txt`, `035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/scratch/shape-check.txt` | The cited files carry the 22 start lines, the 10 decline lines, the 11 pre/final data lines, the 2326-passed suite line and the mutation check of the new summary case. |\n101: \n102: ### Overlay Protocols\n103: \n104: | Protocol | Status | Iteration | Reason |\n105: |---|---|---|---|\n106: | `skill_agent` | notApplicable | 3 | No skill file under `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor` names the scorer; only the folder README does. |\n107: | `agent_cross_runtime` | notApplicable | 3 | No agent definition in `.skilled/agents/` or a runtime mirror names the scorer. |\n108: | `feature_catalog_code` | notApplicable | 3 | The scorer is a measurement script with no catalog row. |\n109: | `playbook_capability` | notApplicable | 3 | No playbook capability names the scorer. |\n110: \n111: ### AC_COVERAGE\n112: \n113: Advisory and not machine-run by this lineage: `validate.sh` is outside the permitted commands for a detached lineage. Read by hand, every 036 acceptance row is `Met` with the evidence this report cites, so the signal is expected to pass when the packet is validated at the merge.\n114: \n115: ## 8. Deferred Items\n116: \n117: - The numeric restatement of 007 and 033 is accepted from the packet's own `scratch/` evidence, not re-scored here.\n118: - The duplicated start rule (`startShape` versus `startedCommand`) is recorded as a follow-on risk, not a finding: the two agree today and two instances do not justify a shared helper under the repository's restraint rule.\n119: - A missing fresh row file makes the scorer file fresh runs as `unknown_row` rather than refusing; that path predates this branch and is recorded here, not raised.\n120: \n121: ## Dimension Expansion Map\n122: \n123: | Dimension | Iterations | Result |\n124: |---|---|---|\n125: | correctness | 1 | Two P2: multi-heredoc false write; unnamed write counted as inside the checkout |\n126: | security | 2 | No finding: holdout rows are refused before a session loads, and no printed line carries prompt text |\n127: | traceability | 2 | One P2: the old cat-counts rule survives in the README row and the shell-step comment |\n128: | maintainability | 3 | One P2: `scoreRun`'s return declaration omits `startShape` |\n129: \n130: ## 9. Search Ledger\n131: \n132: | Search | Method | Result | Disposition |\n133: |---|---|---|---|\n134: | Heredoc stripping and redirect scanning | direct read + `node --input-type=module -e` probe over `normalize` | Empty body, backslash end word and opening-line redirect behave as documented; a two-delimiter line leaves the second body scannable | finding `iter1-P2-second-heredoc-body-write` |\n135: | Write boundary and the read-alone rule | direct read + probe over `startState`/`startedCommand` | A read plus an unnamed write returns `readWrite`; a read plus an outside-checkout write returns `readOnly` | finding `iter1-P2-unnamed-write-is-inside-checkout`; the outside-checkout case ruled in favour of the code |\n136: | Start-shape tally invariant | direct read of `scoreRun`, `addScored`, `tallyBlock` | The four starting shapes sum to `started`; `readOnly` holds the lookups | clean |\n137: | Holdout hygiene | direct read of `loadRowLabels`, `scoreRun`, every `process.stdout.write` line | Holdout rows are marked and refused before a session loads; output carries ids, codes and counts | clean |\n138: | Docs against code | read of the README row and the shell-step comment | Both keep the old rule in one place | finding `iter2-P2-old-start-rule-still-stated` |\n139: | Packet checklist evidence | read of the 036 and 035 `scratch/` files | Counts match the criteria's data lines; mutation check recorded | clean |\n140: | Producer/consumer contract | read of `scoreRun`'s `@returns`, the object it builds and `addScored` | `startShape` is missing from the declaration | finding `iter3-P2-score-run-return-omits-start-shape` |\n141: \n142: ## 10. Audit Appendix\n143: \n144: ### Iteration Records\n145: \n146: | Iteration | Focus | Findings | Ratio | Verdict | Gateway receipt |\n147: |---|---|---|---|---|---|\n148: | 1 | correctness | 2 P2 | 1.0 | PASS | ledger sequence 2, `event-588468c9` |\n149: | 2 | security and traceability | 1 P2 | 0.3333 | PASS | ledger sequence 3, `event-96a8b6c6` |\n150: | 3 | maintainability | 1 P2 | 0.25 | PASS | ledger sequence 4, `event-5d31c238` |\n151: \n152: ### Core Protocols Appendix\n153: \n154: - `spec_code`: iteration 1 recorded the mapping from phase 036 REQ-004 to `startState` and its cases; iteration 3 re-read the same lines while checking the contract.\n155: - `checklist_evidence`: iteration 2 read the four `scratch/` files named by the 035 and 036 criteria; iteration 3 carried the result.\n156: \n157: ### Overlay Protocols Appendix\n158: \n159: - All four overlay protocols resolve `notApplicable` in iteration 3, each with the read that shows no skill, agent, catalog row or playbook capability names the scorer.\n160: \n161: ### State Integrity\n162: \n163: - Three iteration narratives, three delta files, three canonical records and three receipted ledger appends agree on iteration number, focus, dimension set and finding ids.\n164: - `deep-review-state.jsonl` is the gateway's projection; the lineage never wrote it directly.\n165: - The reducer ran after each iteration (exit 0) and owns the registry, the dashboard and the anchored strategy blocks.\n166: - The registry's `dimension` for `iter2-P2-old-start-rule-still-stated` reads `security` while its finding class is `traceability`: the reducer derives a finding's dimension from the first dimension name in the iteration focus, and iteration 2's focus names security first. The finding's own `dimension` and class in `findingDetails` and in `deltas/iter-002.jsonl` are `traceability`.\n167: - No file outside `review/lineages/scorer-6/` was created or modified by this lineage, and no review target file was touched; `git status --porcelain -- .skilled` is empty.\n168: \n169: ### Holdout Statement\n170: \n171: No corpus, holdout or fresh prompt file was opened by this lineage. The probes imported the scorer module and passed crafted records in memory; the only evidence reads were the packet's `scratch/` text files and the packet's acceptance criteria."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-6/review-report.md\"}"},"time":{"